  "notes": [
    "Git HEAD 7cdd1df7d98a53938aa4a546993daae6eabddb78. Served build = local build of main: production index-D5DBubp7.js equals a fresh local npm run build (dist/assets/index-D5DBubp7.js, index-M-cio8KZ.css).",
    "Production honours ?wiTest=1 (main.ts installs window.__wiTest on the world route whenever the flag is present; not gated on DEV), so the check read owner(), stale() and lastLanding() through it.",
    "The window manager placed the 1920x1080 window maximized at (0,35), 1920x1045; the viewport was 1920x958 @1 (not fullscreen, so a real Esc would not also leave fullscreen). Mode B needs >= 1000 px of width: each half was 960 px.",
    "Mode A (step 2 batch / step 6 mesh): the overlay showed 155 / 155 ms after M; the map's tiles covered more than half of the 1575x897 view 84 / 23 ms after the overlay showed (tilesDrawnMs); the Density drawer's slice showed its size 525 / 577 ms after the drawer was opened (sliceMs).",
    "RD 8 (225 columns revealed at the spawn and after each refill). Teleport: landingMs, the time from the click until the landing callback fired and the overlay closed, was 32 ms (batch) / 22 ms (mesh). In the HUD's revealed count, sampled every 250 ms from the click: the old place was gone (0 revealed) by 295 / 284 ms, the new place grew from 548 / 791 ms, reached half of its final count at 1055 / 1551 ms and was at 225 / 225 at 15 s.",
    "lastLatencyMs (step 4): in mode B, edit → preview, from the input event. Samples 19, 160, 136, 26, 14, 16 ms, max 160 ms: the climate.C wavelength edits 160, 136 ms; the density edits and their undo/redo 14-26 ms, since they do not change the biome layer's tiles. The previews land within about the 150 ms quiet window (the session change → the Apply, measured at 154-159 ms in step 9), so they run mostly while the world is held (the aux lane may use all 6 workers); the 160 ms sample likely ended at or just after the Apply, its tail under the capped rule. None measures a level-256 preview running the whole way under cap 1. The mesh edit (step 6) read 22 ms (information only). By the spec §6.4/§13 rule as written (lastLatencyMs > 500 ms builds the cache) cutLineCache reads SP10. capRegime (step 9) measures a related case, a map pan of level-4 tiles right after an Apply.",
    "Esc (spec 2.4) in headful Chrome, with a CDP-injected Esc: the lock was released and the keydown did not reach the page (no Escape keydown or keyup reached a capture-phase window listener installed before it, while the W keydown/keyup during the same lock did); the map then owned the controls with the overlay and the Density drawer still open. A real Esc is the user's check; Firefox is the user's run.",
    "Selftest 59/59 (✓ all 59 goldens match (7.6 s)). Beforeunload dialogs (leaving an edited world for the next load and for ?selftest=1) were accepted through CDP Page.handleJavaScriptDialog: 9-cap-regime, 6-mesh, 7-selftest; ignored log: the favicon.ico 404. Page errors 0, other console errors 0.",
    "capRegime (step 9: a fresh batch load in mode B, run between steps 5 and 6, with a worker job log and a map draw log installed in our page for that load only): 12 level-4 map tiles in the 615x870 map view at 4 blocks/px (tilesInView per pan 12, 16, 12, 15, 16, 12); each pan dragged the view by more than its width plus one tile, to ground with no cached tile (cachedBefore 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0). Pointer-up → the first draw showing every view tile: at rest 1460, 2210, 1672 ms; right after the Apply was issued (density.detailAmpHi, T pending) 3476, 3382, 2847 ms. T (the last terrain reply) finished 1516, 1521, 1393 ms after pointer-up; view tiles that landed while T was still pending: 1, 2, 2; most map-tile jobs running at once while T was pending 1, 1, 1, after T 6, 6, 6, at rest 6, 6, 6; the world still regenerating (a world job unanswered) when the pan's last tile was drawn: false, false, false. These during-Apply pan times mix two regimes: T stayed pending for only 1516, 1521, 1393 ms after pointer-up, and only 1, 2, 2 of the view's tiles landed under cap 1; the rest (about 51-56 % of each pan's time) ran after T with 6 tiles at once. The cap-1 rate seen is one level-4 tile at a time at about 700 ms each; at RD 8, T lasts about 1.5 s, so a pan right after an Apply waits about that long longer than at rest. tilesInView differs per pan (12, 16, 12 at rest; 15, 16, 12 during), so compare the per-tile figures; the baselines always ran first, while the load rose.",
    "Per tile (a level-4 tile's worker run, post → reply): median 673.4 ms at rest (n 43), 700.8 ms during the Apply (n 44); pan time per view tile 121.7, 138.1, 139.3 ms at rest, 231.7, 211.4, 237.3 ms during the Apply.",
    "Straddle: climate.C.wavelength 2400 → 2000, then → 2800, the second commit 204 ms after the first; the stale count first rose (an Apply issued) 155 ms after the first commit; two configures posted, 1 ms and 207 ms after it (the second to the 6 workers across a millisecond boundary); lastLatencyMs of the second 112 ms."
