    "notes": [
      "Every map-tile job the pans posted was level 4 (mapTileJobs.byLevel): the view's own level at 4 blocks/px (planTiles priority 1000 + dist). The 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 1 level-256 preview tiles under each view were already cached, so no pan posted a level-256 job; spec 6.4's \"about 54 ms\" is a level-256 tile, these are level-4 tiles (median worker run 673.4 ms at rest, 700.8 ms during the Apply).",
      "Apply issued: the pan's drag began once __wiTest.stale() rose above 0 (commitToApplyMs 159, 158, 154 ms after the Enter); pointer-up came 54, 34, 39 ms after that; stale() at pointer-up 225, 225, 225, the HUD row read just after the pan 225/225, 225/225, 218/225. T pending is read from the job log (terrain jobs still unanswered), not from the page.",
      "Aux policy: not exposed by the page; observed as concurrency in the job log. While T was pending at most 1, 1, 1 map-tile job ran at once (all aux jobs: 2, 2, 2, the extra one an interactive hover point job, priority < 0, outside the cap); after T, 6, 6, 6; at rest 6, 6, 6 of 6 pool workers. The page has 7 Worker objects; jobs went to 6.",
      "The Density drawer was closed for step 9 (a fresh load opens it closed; the drawer state is not persisted), so no slice job competed with the tiles.",
      "Straddle: the stale count rose (an Apply issued) 155 ms after the first commit, before the second commit at 204 ms; configures were posted 1, 207, 208 ms after the first commit; every terrain job posted afterwards carried one epoch (5: 465 jobs, first posted 777 ms after the first commit). The second edit's preview (lastLatencyMs 112 ms) followed its own configure, so the pool's epoch again differed from the applied generation while it ran (the held rule, cap = n).",
      "The job log closes a job at its reply or, when the pool posts the next job to the same worker first (its onmessage runs before our listener), at that post; the draw log counts drawImage calls of the target tile size per full-canvas redraw. Both add a few function calls per message or draw in our page only."
